  "paragraphs": [
    "Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play.",
    "Maqam Sikah Baladi is arguably the most challenging Arabic maqam. Its scale (and sayr) is something of a hybrid between a transposition of Maqam Huzam to an ordinary non-Sikah note, and Maqam Hijazkar – the intervals are not quite the same as either, but it sounds a bit like both. None of its intervals match either just or equal-tempered intonation, making it impossible to reproduce on anything but the voice and traditional Arabic instruments.",
    "Maqam Sikah Baladi is not part of a maqam family.",
    "Watch a 1-minute sample Violin Taqsim in Maqam Sikah Baladi by Sami Abu Shumays."
  ],
  "text": "Maqam Sikah Baladi (not part of a maqam family) Maqam Index Pronunciation of Sikah Baladi Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play. Maqam Sikah Baladi is arguably the most challenging Arabic maqam. Its scale (and sayr) is something of a hybrid between a transposition of Maqam Huzam to an ordinary non-Sikah note, and Maqam Hijazkar – the intervals are not quite the same as either, but it sounds a bit like both. None of its intervals match either just or equal-tempered intonation, making it impossible to reproduce on anything but the voice and traditional Arabic instruments . Maqam Sikah Baladi is not part of a maqam family. Watch a 1-minute sample Violin Taqsim in Maqam Sikah Baladi by Sami Abu Shumays. Sahirtu Minhu al-Layali (1935) Vocals and Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Kulli Da Kan Leh (1954) Vocals and Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) el-Habib el-Majhul(1972) Vocals and Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) al-Karnak (1941) Vocals and Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Shams el-Asil (1958) Umm Kulthum Music by Riyad al-Sunbati el-Hobb Kida (1959) Umm Kulthum Music by Riyad al-Sunbati Yalli Kan Yishgik Anini (1949) Umm Kulthum Music by Riyad al-Sunbati Aruh Li Min (1958) Umm Kulthum Music by Riyad al-Sunbati Taqsim Buzuq Matar Muhammad (Lebanon) Taqsim Qanun Abraham Salman (Iraq) Saltanah",
